\title{Example relations which are transitive}
\date{2026-02-28T23:02:13Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{The only relations among [our examples](008E) which are \em{not} transitive are #{R_4} and #{R_5}. All the rest are transitive. We use the transitivity of these relations all the time! For example, transitivity of #{=} is what allows us to prove #{X = Y} by showing a chain of equalities #{X = X_1 = X_2 = \dots = Y}.}
